---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = "Addictions & Substance Use | AOC, Calgary";
const description = "Explore questions about alcohol, substance use and change with Alex Orlando Counselling in Calgary.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="wrap"><section class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">Addictions & substance use</div><h1>Look beyond the pattern.<br>Make room for change.</h1><p class="lead">Questions about substance use can be complicated. There is room to explore them without reducing your story to a label.</p></section><div class="content-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>What does change<br>mean to you?</h2><p>You might be questioning your use, concerned about its impact, returning to a goal after a setback, or unsure whether you want to change at all.</p><p>The proposed AOC approach starts with understanding your experience, your priorities, and the support that fits your situation.</p><h3>Questions worth exploring</h3><ul><li>What do you turn to substances for, and what are the costs?</li><li>When does use feel more difficult to manage?</li><li>What would you want to be different in daily life?</li><li>Which relationships and supports could help?</li></ul><h3>Finding appropriate care</h3><p>Counselling is one possible part of a broader support plan. Medical assessment, withdrawal support, peer support, or other services may also be relevant. The right next step depends on your situation.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.albertahealthservices.ca/amh/amh.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Alberta addiction & mental health services ↗</a></div><aside class="side-box"><h3>You can begin with uncertainty</h3><p>Having mixed feelings does not prevent you from asking questions. You can explore options without making every decision at once.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Consultation details ↗</a></aside></div></div></main>
</Layout>
